,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/1590f53ae96ac625bdae3e1815cc93bda067270c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/365139a51c3b6f5f3df8832ad4008cd3ed185ec8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T13:32:40Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T13:32:40Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"refactor(retrieval): dedupe the fusion-weight validator into vector_store.base (AR006)\n\nRigor AR006 flagged _validate_weight (fusion.py) and _validate_non_negative_weight\n(composite.py) as duplicate bodies — they are byte-identical non-negative-weight\nvalidators. Move the single implementation to vector_store/base.py as the public\nvalidate_non_negative_weight and import it in both; base.py has no back-edge to\nfusion/composite, so no import cycle. Behaviour unchanged (539 retrieval/fusion/\ncomposite tests green).\n\nValidated the other two AR006 and all nine AR001 rigor findings rather than\nmechanically \"fixing\" them — they are unsafe or false positives:\n- AR006 _hash_bag (continual_adversarial.scorer vs self_evolving.trainer): bodies\n  are identical but bind to DIFFERENT accelerators (_RUST_CONTINUAL_ADV vs\n  _RUST_SELF_EVOLVING) and different mandatory_execution(__name__) scopes; sharing\n  one copy would change the accelerator wiring and the ADR-0001 bit-exact path.\n  Not a safe dedup — left in place.\n- AR006 _first / _first_present (ui): a trivial 5-line dict lookup with different\n  call conventions (varargs vs tuple); consolidating adds a module and net LOC for\n  no real benefit. Left in place.\n- AR001 import cycles (9): all already broken at RUNTIME via the correct Python\n  idioms — TYPE_CHECKING guards (e.g. core.types -> safety_event) and function-local\n  lazy imports (e.g. core.license -> polar_license, scoring._nli_export -> nli). The\n  package imports cleanly with no runtime cycle; rigor''s static AST analysis counts\n  the guarded/lazy references anyway. Not bugs; breaking them further would be a\n  large, risky, no-benefit refactor. No action.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"cc0d60edfd280cbbfe11f572d1e82af654715a27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/cc0d60edfd280cbbfe11f572d1e82af654715a27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/365139a51c3b6f5f3df8832ad4008cd3ed185ec8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/365139a51c3b6f5f3df8832ad4008cd3ed185ec8","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDM2NTEzOWE1MWMzYjZmNWYzZGY4ODMyYWQ0MDA4Y2QzZWQxODVlYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654","sha":"eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654"}],"sha":"365139a51c3b6f5f3df8832ad4008cd3ed185ec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/365139a51c3b6f5f3df8832ad4008cd3ed185ec8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T12:38:22Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T12:38:22Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"fix(compliance): enforce RFC 5280 CA constraints + sole-critical TSA EKU in the anchor chain validator\n\nAddresses the CEO distinct-identity second-eye on f553e4e7 (Findings 1 + 2 on\n_chain_to_trusted_root).\n\nFinding 1 (MEDIUM, path-validation flaw): cryptography''s\nverify_directly_issued_by checks only issuer-name + signature — NOT\nbasicConstraints CA=True, KeyUsage.keyCertSign, or pathLenConstraint. Because the\nintermediate certificates come from the attacker-controlled token, a leaked\nNON-CA end-entity key E could forge a time-stamping leaf L and present L<-E<-root,\nwhich would validate. Add `_valid_ca_issuer`: every candidate issuer (each\nintermediate AND the pinned root) must have basicConstraints CA=True, must not\nexceed its pathLenConstraint for the number of subordinate CAs below it, and — when\na KeyUsage extension is present — must assert keyCertSign, before it is accepted as\nan issuer.\n\nFinding 2 (LOW, RFC 3161 §2.3): the leaf EKU check now requires the extended key\nusage to be EXACTLY {id-kp-timeStamping} and marked critical, rejecting a leaf that\ncarries time-stamping among other usages or a non-critical EKU.\n\nTests: the non-CA-intermediate forgery (no basicConstraints and explicit CA=False),\nKeyUsage without keyCertSign, pathLenConstraint exceeded, multi-EKU leaf, and\nnon-critical EKU leaf are all now rejected; a KeyUsage-with-keyCertSign CA still\nchains. 100% line+branch on the module retained; bandit / semgrep / mypy / ruff /\ntypos clean. The trusted-roots path was default-off and not operator-enabled, so no\nprod anchor relied on the weaker check.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"87235b3bc5eedecf4b81ffa155174259e0f69ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/87235b3bc5eedecf4b81ffa155174259e0f69ea0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKGViNmEyMmJiYTVmOGRjMjQwM2E0YzAyNjY3NTEwMWY3OWY0NmQ2NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d","sha":"f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d"}],"sha":"eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/eb6a22bba5f8dc2403a4c026675101f79f46d654"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T12:23:58Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T12:23:58Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"feat(compliance): root-of-trust pinning for RFC 3161 anchor verification (KIMI3-anchoring)\n\nCompletes the KIMI3-anchoring follow-up the CEO recorded: verify_token can now\nchain the embedded TSA signing certificate to operator-configured trusted TSA\nroots, upgrading the guarantee from \"some certificate attested this digest at\ngenTime\" (TSA-token-anchored) to \"a trusted TSA attested it\"\n(trusted-TSA-attested) and completing back-dating resistance.\n\n- verify_token(anchor, hash, *, trusted_roots=None): after the four existing\n  fail-closed checks, when trusted_roots is a non-empty list the signing cert\n  must chain to a pinned root — validated at the token''s genTime, with the\n  time-stamping EKU on the leaf and every cert on the path time-valid.\n  trusted_roots=None keeps today''s internal-consistency-only behaviour,\n  byte-identical (backward compatible).\n- No new dependency: the chain is built with cryptography''s\n  verify_directly_issued_by (issuer-name + signature) + not_valid_*_utc + EKU\n  access; the TLS-only x509.verification.PolicyBuilder is the wrong fit for the\n  TSA (EKU=timeStamping) case. No revocation / name-constraint checking — trust\n  is anchored on the pinned root.\n- Fixed a latent CMS bug surfaced by multi-cert tokens: the signer certificate\n  is now located by the SignerInfo sid (issuer + serial) instead of position [0].\n  CMS `certificates` is a SET and DER reorders it, so [0] was not reliably the\n  signer; this corrects both the signature check and the chain leaf. Single-cert\n  self-signed tokens were unaffected, which is why the earlier land passed.\n- load_trusted_roots(pem) parses a PEM root bundle (fail-closed on\n  missing/invalid). Config audit_anchor_tsa_roots (env\n  DIRECTOR_AUDIT_ANCHOR_TSA_ROOTS). CLI `verify-anchors --tsa-roots PEM` states\n  whether verification was root-pinned (trusted-TSA-attested) or token-only.\n  AnchorStore.verify_against_chain threads the roots through.\n\nTests: extended the in-process synthetic TSA with a CA-issued leaf (+ intermediate)\npath — root-pinned / intermediate-chain / untrusted-root / expired-at-genTime /\nmissing-EKU / self-signed-rejected-under-pinning / signer-not-in-token /\ndepth-bound cases, all no-network. 100% line+branch on the module retained;\nbandit / semgrep / mypy / ruff / typos clean; capability + studio manifests\nunchanged.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"e711712a721c19757a25d931fdcbd4d24d269060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/e711712a721c19757a25d931fdcbd4d24d269060"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKGY1NTNlNGU3N2VkMzUzMzU5ZDUwOTg3ZWE1MGZiNTJiNWQ1ODg0MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f","sha":"53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f"}],"sha":"f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/f553e4e77ed353359d50987ea50fb52b5d58841d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:50:31Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:52:35Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"fix(sast): reject non-http(s) TSA URLs + silence the Semgrep dynamic-urllib finding\n\nSemgrep''s python.lang.security.audit.dynamic-urllib-use-detected (the same\nfile:// read vector Bandit B310 flags) blocked SAST on the anchor client''s\nurllib POST. Close the vector for real: _default_transport now refuses any TSA\nURL whose scheme is not http(s) before calling urlopen, so a mis-set value\ncannot become a local-file read. With that guard the urlopen is safe, so the\nline carries the standard tri-tool suppression (noqa S310 / nosec B310 /\nnosemgrep). New test covers the file:// rejection.\n\nVerified locally: semgrep scan (p/python + p/security-audit) = 0 findings;\nbandit = 0; ruff clean; the module stays 100% line+branch.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"1d63958afd258840b118cce2b4945b8cf6f5a872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/1d63958afd258840b118cce2b4945b8cf6f5a872"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDUzZDE2ZDY1ZWZjZDA1ZWFlOTVmMmMzOTg0NDE3NThiNjc0NWRlOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac","sha":"6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac"}],"sha":"53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/53d16d65efcd05eae95f2c398441758b6745de9f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:30:59Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T04:30:59Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"fix(ci): install asn1crypto in the test env + silence Bandit false positives\n\nThe push CI on 4eb267d6 exposed two gaps the local run missed:\n\n1. Test env. tests/test_timestamp_anchor.py imports asn1crypto at module level,\n   but the base `test` job installs only requirements/ci-dev.txt (the [dev]\n   extra), which did not include asn1crypto — collection failed with\n   ModuleNotFoundError on every Python version. The base `test` job is the only\n   pytest runner (the test-extras jobs are import-smoke only), so the module\n   would otherwise never be exercised in CI. Add `director-ai[crypto]` to the\n   [dev] extra (mirroring the existing `director-ai[rust]`), add the asn1crypto\n   entry to ci-dev.txt (verified hashes), and re-lock uv.lock. cryptography was\n   already present transitively.\n\n2. Bandit. Two findings on timestamp_anchor.py, both false positives, silenced\n   inline: B310 on the operator-configured urllib TSA POST (the URL is a\n   deployment config value, not attacker-controlled), and B105 on the literal\n   \"sha256\" (a hash-algorithm name, not a secret).\n\nNo behaviour change; 100% line+branch on the module retained.\n\nVerified: https://pypi.org/pypi/asn1crypto/1.5.1/json\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"132668bec0123b408aab07a6a2946a403633eb8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/132668bec0123b408aab07a6a2946a403633eb8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDZlNjMwN2ZhMzgwN2NiNTdlNzhhMGZiYzM0YjEzNmY3MWI2ZTc5YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c","sha":"4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c"}],"sha":"6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6e6307fa3807cb57e78a0fbc34b136f71b6e79ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:50:39Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:50:39Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"refine(compliance): tighten timestamp-anchor verify + honest scope (CEO second-eye)\n\nApplies the two non-blocking asks from the CEO distinct-identity second-eye on\n6169c87d:\n\n(a) Scope the claims honestly. verify_token proves the token is signed by the\n    certificate IT CARRIES over our digest — \"some certificate attested this\n    time\" — not that a TRUSTED TSA did; without chaining to a configured TSA\n    root, back-dating resistance depends on the certificate being trusted out of\n    band. The module/verify_token docstrings and the CHANGELOG now say\n    \"TSA-token-anchored, root-pinning follow-up\" and drop the stronger\n    \"cannot back-date without forging a TSA signature\" phrasing. Root-of-trust\n    pinning stays the documented follow-up that upgrades this to\n    \"trusted-TSA-attested\".\n\n(b) Full CMS strictness: verify_token now also checks the content-type signed\n    attribute == id-ct-TSTInfo (belt-and-braces alongside the existing\n    encapsulated content-type check), reading the signed attributes into a dict\n    so a missing attribute reads as None and fails closed. New test covers a\n    token whose signed content-type attribute lies while the encapsulated\n    content is a valid TSTInfo.\n\n100% line+branch on the module retained. No change to the anchoring path;\nverification only got stricter.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"61a92a7645bd0e416181b3116810ded8fe6a3f08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/61a92a7645bd0e416181b3116810ded8fe6a3f08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDRlYjI2N2Q2NDkwY2E4N2Y5OTViYmYwZGYzMjY4ZjYyZjQ5YzY1MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94","sha":"b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94"}],"sha":"4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/4eb267d6490ca87f995bbf0df3268f62f49c650c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:41:59Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:41:59Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"fix(test): reword comment to satisfy the CI typos hook\n\nThe pre-commit `typos` hook flags the bare `mis` in \"mis-dispatch\" (a\nhyphenated-prefix false positive); reword the Ed25519 unsupported-key test\ncomment. No behaviour change.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"a84f5b89b690691734616f9ffe8cffe9c194dc96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/a84f5b89b690691734616f9ffe8cffe9c194dc96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKGIwNGVhY2NhMDI5NmYyYmY3NTA1ZjZmYjRiZGUwMTYwZmUxNjFhOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00","sha":"6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00"}],"sha":"b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/b04eacca0296f2bf7505f6fb4bde0160fe161a94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:37:35Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:37:35Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"feat(compliance): RFC 3161 external timestamp anchoring for the audit chain (KIMI3-anchoring)\n\nThe compliance audit hash chain (compliance/audit_log.py) proves\ntamper-evidence but not existence-at-time: whoever holds the HMAC secret can\nrebuild the chain with back-dated timestamps. This closes that gap with\nRFC 3161.\n\nNew compliance/timestamp_anchor.py obtains a trusted-timestamp token from a\nTimestamp Authority over the current chain head (which, through the prev_hash\nlinkage, commits to the whole prior history), verifies it — message-imprint\nbinding, the CMS signature over the signed attributes against the embedded TSA\ncertificate (RSA or ECDSA; unsupported key types fail closed), and the\nmessage-digest attribute — and stores it in an audit_anchor table. A verified\nanchor proves the chain existed at or before the TSA''s genTime; the keyholder\ncannot back-date past it without forging a TSA signature.\n\n- AuditLog.current_head() exposes the chain head (the only change to the chain\n  module; anchoring stays decoupled, so asn1crypto never enters audit_log''s\n  import graph).\n- director-ai compliance anchor / verify-anchors drive it from the CLI, the\n  natural surface for a periodic, out-of-band operation. The paid BUSL import\n  is function-local so the free CLI file never loads it at module import.\n- Opt-in and offline-graceful: audit_anchor_enabled (default off),\n  audit_anchor_tsa_url, audit_anchor_timeout_s; try_anchor_chain_head logs a\n  warning and returns None on a down/unreachable TSA, never raising into the\n  audit path.\n- Publishing to a public transparency log (Rekor) is deliberately out of scope\n  (a separate outward-facing decision).\n\nDependency: adds asn1crypto (>=1.5,<2) to the [crypto] extra — cryptography\nalone cannot build a TimeStampReq or parse a TSTInfo. The import is lazy and\nimport-guarded (AnchorDependencyError with an install hint), so the free/core\nsurface never pulls it; the paid tiers reach it through director-ai[crypto].\nmypy: asn1crypto added to the ignore_missing_imports overrides (no py.typed).\n\nTests: tests/test_timestamp_anchor.py mints a synthetic TSA in-process\n(self-signed RSA and EC certificates, real CMS SignedData over a real TSTInfo)\nand drives the anchorer, verifier, store and CLI end-to-end through an injected\ntransport — 100% line+branch on the new module, no network. Regenerated the\ncapability and studio manifests for the new module and test.\n\nVerified: https://pypi.org/pypi/asn1crypto/1.5.1/json\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"aec02f269c81f7d45d3e65b46a6ba3b559fa0080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/aec02f269c81f7d45d3e65b46a6ba3b559fa0080"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDYxNjljODdkZDM0MWY4ZGY4NGU3ZTZlY2MzNjVkYzNlMTk2NGZjMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51","sha":"65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51"}],"sha":"6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/6169c87dd341f8df84e7e6ecc365dc3e1964fc00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T00:37:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T00:37:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"fix(deps): bump grpc-go to v1.82.1 in gateway/go (GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf)\n\nResolves dependabot HIGH #350 (GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf, \"gRPC-Go: xDS RBAC and\nHTTP/2 Vulnerabilities\"). google.golang.org/grpc was v1.79.3, in the\nvulnerable range < 1.82.1; bump to the first patched version v1.82.1 via\n`go get` + `go mod tidy`. Transitive genproto/googleapis/rpc and\ngoogle.golang.org/protobuf (1.36.10 -> 1.36.11) follow; the `go` directive\nis unchanged (1.25.0). gateway/go is the only Go module in the tree.\n\nLocal validation (gateway/go, Go 1.25 via GOTOOLCHAIN=auto): go build ./...,\ngo vet ./..., and go test ./... all pass (9 packages green). CI builds\ngateway/go, so push-then-CI reconfirms on the runner.\n\nVerified: https://proxy.golang.org/google.golang.org/grpc/@v/v1.82.1.info (v1.82.1, refs/tags/v1.82.1, 2026-07-15T23:31:12Z, hash ebd8f06a)\nVerified: https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/security/dependabot/350 (GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf, first_patched 1.82.1)\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"aaf3d06e9824569cf5ab88f32343f94327ee2a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/aaf3d06e9824569cf5ab88f32343f94327ee2a17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKDY1YmExMWQ1NTBjNTI5YmQwOTMyZjU4OGUxYTIyMjcxYzc4ZmFmNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf","sha":"d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf"}],"sha":"65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/65ba11d550c529bd0932f588e1a22271c78faf51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T00:07:02Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T00:07:02Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"ci(publish): fail closed with a clear error on a missing release tag\n\nThe publish workflows resolve RELEASE_TAG from the release event or the\nworkflow_dispatch `tag` input, then actions/checkout uses it as `ref`.\nWhen dispatched without a tag (the input''s `required` flag is enforced by\nthe UI form, not the dispatch API), RELEASE_TAG was empty and checkout\nfailed cryptically with `fatal: invalid refspec` after three retries —\nobserved in run 29878820898 (benign: it died before build/publish).\n\nAdd a \"Validate release tag\" guard as the first step in publish.yml,\npublish-lite.yml and publish-paid.yml. It fails immediately with an\nexplicit, actionable message when RELEASE_TAG is empty or is not a vX.Y.Z\ntag, instead of the opaque checkout error. Fail-closed and additive; it\nnever blocks a real release (a v* tag from the release event or an explicit\ndispatch input still passes). RELEASE_TAG is read as a shell env var, not\ninterpolated, so a hostile tag name cannot inject.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"f590c8bcebcab3ebb9f89838f53c870b14f4e633","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/f590c8bcebcab3ebb9f89838f53c870b14f4e633"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf","node_id":"C_kwDORQ8Eq9oAKGQ1NTk1ZDdiMTVkMDY3ZTgxYmU0ZWE0ODFhMGU1YWI3YmQ5NjMyYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/director-ai/commit/3fb17983137c13719dff6e8ab97bee48cc54efab","sha":"3fb17983137c13719dff6e8ab97bee48cc54efab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/3fb17983137c13719dff6e8ab97bee48cc54efab"}],"sha":"d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/d5595d7b15d067e81be4ea481a0e5ab7bd9632bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/3fb17983137c13719dff6e8ab97bee48cc54efab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T23:23:01Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T23:23:01Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"ci(release): auto-dispatch PyPI publish on tag (one-click, no PAT)\n\nrelease.yml built the GitHub Release but never triggered the publish\nworkflows, because a GITHUB_TOKEN-created Release does not emit\nrelease:published (GitHub anti-recursion) — so every release needed a\nmanual `gh workflow run publish.yml -f tag=...` (hit again shipping\nv3.19.0 tonight).\n\nAdd a dispatch-publish job that fires publish.yml / publish-lite.yml /\npublish-paid.yml via workflow_dispatch — the documented EXCEPTION to the\nGITHUB_TOKEN anti-recursion rule — so no RELEASE_PAT is needed and each\npublish workflow still runs AS ITSELF, preserving its own PyPI\ntrusted-publisher OIDC identity (we never publish from release.yml). The\njob first detects RELEASE_PAT and SKIPS the dispatch when it is set, so the\nauto-chain path never double-uploads.\n\nInert until the next v* tag push. Rust wheels (wheels.yml) stay a separate\nmanual/optional lane, matching current practice.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"f45621a08c71e0517481eee6af785f821a8c71fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/f45621a08c71e0517481eee6af785f821a8c71fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/3fb17983137c13719dff6e8ab97bee48cc54efab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":