s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/commits/55d30e3b8c5d365ac9a28b3b70e2876c1b706780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T20:24:24Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T20:24:24Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Arcane Sapience"},"message":"docs: lead with one accuracy number, split the newcomer nav funnel\n\n- index.md feature grid: the AggreFact cell led with four accuracy numbers\n  at once (75.6 / 75.8 / 77.76 at different thresholds). It now leads with\n  the 75.6% leaderboard figure plus the 77.76% tuned result; the\n  75.8%-at-0.46 operating point moves to the Scoring methodology page.\n- mkdocs nav: \"Getting Started\" carried twelve entries, eight of them\n  positioning essays that drowned Quickstart. Split into a lean\n  \"Getting Started\" (Quickstart, Installation, Notebook Gallery, Product\n  Overview, Onboarding, Runtime Boundaries) and a new \"Why & Positioning\"\n  section for the market/comparison pages. Every page stays reachable\n  (mkdocs --strict clean).\n- applications-and-market-map: cross-linked the public-vs-commercial\n  boundary table to the full pricing ladder.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"954ec1ec3684dc9e02bb88e2eda097d7d46c3249","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/trees/954ec1ec3684dc9e02bb88e2eda097d7d46c3249"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/director-ai/git/commits/55d30e3b8c5d365ac9a28b3b70e2876c1b706780","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"ava