users/CODEXY-ofi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CODEXY-ofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CODEXY-ofi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CODEXY-ofi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adriangmrraa/clinicforge/commits/a5d406f8b400513b8045c2f18eff3edee1df6bbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T20:45:01Z","email":"contact@codexyoficial.com","name":"CODEXY-ofi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T20:45:58Z","email":"contact@codexyoficial.com","name":"CODEXY-ofi"},"message":"fix(prompt): reprogramar sin contradiccion + loop por franja + paciente habitual\n\n- (D) reprogramar: acotar la prohibicion de reschedule al caso sin-preferencia\n  (2 opciones ofrecidas); ya no contradice el flujo directo cuando el slot\n  pedido esta libre (caso Martin).\n- (E) franja: extender la regla de honestidad — si al pedir otra franja\n  (mañana/tarde) check devuelve los MISMOS slots, no repetirlos como nuevos;\n  ofrecer otro dia (caso Martin, loop).\n- (F) paciente habitual: si el contexto trae \"Obra Social registrada\", no\n  re-preguntar particular/obra social (alinea PASO 2c y REGLA SUPREMA con la\n  REGLA DE COBERTURA existente, caso Laura Altamirano).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a3b0de8e2fdc762b559a2fc6c69da76168b3583","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adriangmrraa/clinicforge/git/trees/5a3b0de8e2fdc762b559a2fc6c69da76168b3583"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adriangmrraa/clinicforge/git/commits/a5d406f8b400513b8045c2f18eff3edee1df6bbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281972831?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CODEXY-ofi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CODEXY-ofi/follow